+# Kerala Police DVAS ΓÇö Endpoint Security Vulnerability & Remediation Report
+
+**Document ID:** `KP-DVAS-SEC-2026-08-17-EP`  
+**Date & Time:** 2026-08-17 01:10:00 PM IST (+05:30)  
+**Target Scope:** Video Ingestion Gateway, Dashboard Backend, Edge Drone Field API, and Session Management  
+**Classification:** Defense-Grade Security Assessment & Vulnerability Remediation Record  
+**Target Audience:** Kerala Police Cyber Command, Security Operations Center (SOC), System Architects  
+
+---
+
+## 1. Executive Summary
+
+During a comprehensive zero-trust audit across all 149 system endpoints in the Kerala Police Drone Video Analytics System (DVAS), several critical endpoint security gaps were identified in the initial architecture baseline. These gaps exposed sensitive tactical drone feeds, live mission controls, and WebSocket telemetry broadcasts to potential eavesdropping, unauthorized mission termination, and cross-origin access.
+
+This document details:
+1. **The Vulnerabilities & Problems Identified** across all endpoints.
+2. **The Operational Impact & Threat Blast Radius** on active police operations.
+3. **Exact Code Locations & Root Causes** in the repository.
+4. **The Engineering Fixes Implemented** with complete Before vs. After code comparisons.
+5. **Live Verification & Retest Results** confirming complete remediation.
+
+---
+
