+### **Vulnerability 4: Unauthenticated Police Mission Termination**
+
+#### **A. Problem Description**
+In the Dashboard backend, `PATCH /api/missions/{mission_id}/end` lacked `user: dict = Depends(get_current_user)`. While all other mission endpoints (`POST`, `PUT`, `GET`) were protected, the termination route was left unauthenticated.
+
+#### **B. Operational Impact & Threat Blast Radius**
+* **Denial of Police Service (DoS):** An unauthenticated actor could send a script to loop over mission IDs (`M_001` through `M_999`) and prematurely mark all active police missions as completed in the database, breaking ongoing incident coordination.
+
+#### **C. Code Location & Root Cause**
+* **File:** [`DVAS_Dashboard/backend/server.py`](file:///d:/DVPS/DVAS_KP/DVAS_Dashboard/backend/server.py#L683-L694)
+* **Root Cause:** Omission of the `Depends(get_current_user)` parameter in the route definition.
+
+#### **D. Technical Remediation**
+1. Added `user: dict = Depends(get_current_user)` to `end_mission_record`.
+2. Added ABAC mission scope enforcement so scoped drone operators can only terminate missions assigned within their authorized district/jurisdiction.
+
+```diff
+--- a/DVAS_Dashboard/backend/server.py
++++ b/DVAS_Dashboard/backend/server.py
+@@ -683,3 +683,8 @@
+ @api.patch("/missions/{mission_id}/end")
+-async def end_mission_record(mission_id: str):
++async def end_mission_record(mission_id: str, user: dict = Depends(get_current_user)):
+     """Mark a mission as completed and record the end time."""
++    # Check jurisdiction / mission scope if user is scoped
++    if user.get("mission_scope") and mission_id not in user["mission_scope"]:
++        raise HTTPException(403, f"Not permitted to end mission {mission_id}")
+```
+
