+### **Vulnerability 6: Unauthenticated Field Drone API & Wildcard CORS**
+
+#### **A. Problem Description**
+The local Field Edge Control server (`dvas_edge/edge_api_server.py`) ran on port `8765` with:
+1. `CORSMiddleware` configured with `allow_origins=["*"]` and `allow_credentials=True`.
+2. 11 API endpoints (`/api/edge/mission/start`, `/api/edge/mission/end`, `/stream/live`, `/api/edge/status`, etc.) completely lacking authentication.
+
+#### **B. Operational Impact & Threat Blast Radius**
+* **Local Field Hijacking:** Any device connecting to the tactical field Wi-Fi router or drone telemetry subnet could start/stop missions, change ingest toggle settings, or snoop on the live camera stream.
+* **Cross-Site Scripting / CSRF Hijacking:** Wildcard CORS with credentials allowed rogue web pages visited by field operators to send authenticated fetch requests to the edge server.
+
+#### **C. Code Location & Root Cause**
+* **File:** [`dvas_edge/edge_api_server.py`](file:///d:/DVPS/DVAS_KP/dvas_edge/edge_api_server.py#L614-L752)
+* **Root Cause:** Unrestricted CORS and absence of authentication guards on field endpoints.
+
+#### **D. Technical Remediation**
+1. Hardened CORS by reading from `CORS_ORIGINS` whitelist, rejecting rogue origin domains.
+2. Built `verify_edge_auth` dependency supporting `X-Edge-API-Key` headers (for automated M2M hardware scripts) and Bearer/Cookie/Query tokens for officer web sessions.
+3. Attached `auth: dict = Depends(verify_edge_auth)` to all 11 edge route handlers.
+
+```diff
+--- a/dvas_edge/edge_api_server.py
++++ b/dvas_edge/edge_api_server.py
+@@ -614,9 +614,14 @@
++_RAW_CORS = os.getenv("CORS_ORIGINS", "http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000,http://localhost:8000,http://localhost:8001")
++CORS_ORIGINS = [origin.strip() for origin in _RAW_CORS.split(",") if origin.strip()]
++app.add_middleware(CORSMiddleware, allow_origins=CORS_ORIGINS, allow_credentials=True, ...)
++
++@app.post("/api/edge/mission/start")
+-def start_mission(req: MissionStartRequest):
++def start_mission(req: MissionStartRequest, auth: dict = Depends(verify_edge_auth)):
+     return pipeline.start_mission(req)
+ 
++@app.get("/stream/live")
+-async def stream_live():
++async def stream_live(auth: dict = Depends(verify_edge_auth)):
+```
+
+---
+
+### **Vulnerability 7: Session Continuity Drop-offs & Browser Token Storage**
+
+#### **A. Problem Description**
+1. Access tokens had a 5-minute lifespan. When the access token expired during long mission planning or case evidence filing, requests immediately failed with `401 Unauthorized`, causing lost form input and force-logging officers out.
+2. Storing access tokens in browser `localStorage` exposed police session tokens to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) exfiltration attacks.
+
+#### **B. Operational Impact & Threat Blast Radius**
+* **Operational Disruption:** Officers in the middle of active tactical operations suffered unexpected session terminations.
+* **Token Hijacking Risk:** Any third-party frontend library vulnerability could read `localStorage` tokens and steal police officer identities.
+
+#### **C. Code Location & Root Cause**
+* **Files:** [`DVAS_Dashboard/frontend/src/context/AuthContext.js`](file:///d:/DVPS/DVAS_KP/DVAS_Dashboard/frontend/src/context/AuthContext.js), [`DVAS_Dashboard/frontend/src/lib/api.js`](file:///d:/DVPS/DVAS_KP/DVAS_Dashboard/frontend/src/lib/api.js), [`DVAS_Dashboard/backend/server.py`](file:///d:/DVPS/DVAS_KP/DVAS_Dashboard/backend/server.py#L308-L365).
+
+#### **D. Technical Remediation**
+1. Removed all `localStorage` token storage; all access and refresh tokens are stored purely in `HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Secure` cookies.
+2. Implemented `POST /api/auth/refresh` on the backend, rotating access tokens using verified refresh tokens.
+3. Added an automated 401 response interceptor in Axios (`api.js`) that silently requests `/api/auth/refresh` and replays the original request seamlessly without interrupting the officer.
+4. On logout (`POST /api/auth/logout`), both cookies are expired immediately with `Max-Age=0`.
+
