+## 1. Executive Summary
+
+A comprehensive Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT) audit was conducted on the **Kerala Police Drone Video Analytics System (DVAS)** to evaluate video streaming pipelines, edge-to-server frame ingestion, real-time WebSocket telemetry broadcasts, and UI session continuity.
+
+Initially, while the **Edge-to-Server Ingestion (`POST /ingest/frame`)** correctly enforced Bearer JWT authentication per frame, **four critical security vulnerabilities** were identified across server-side streaming routes, WebSocket gateways, debug bypass flags, and UI token lifecycles.
+
+All four vulnerabilities have been **remediated in code and behaviorally verified through live adversarial test harnesses** (`test_live_verification_all_4_checks.py` and `test_security_retest.py`), achieving a **100% Pass rate (Exit Code: 0)**.
