+### Finding 4: Unmanaged Access Token Expiration in UI & Data Loss
+
+#### Previous Vulnerable State:
+* **Files:** `DVAS_Dashboard/backend/server.py` & `DVAS_Dashboard/frontend/src/lib/api.js`
+* **Vulnerable Mechanism:** Keycloak issued a 5-minute access token (`accessTokenLifespan = 300`). The backend discarded the refresh token and only stored the access token. After 5 minutes, any form submission or telemetry action failed with `401 Unauthorized`, kicking the user back to `/login` and permanently erasing unsaved form inputs.
+* **Insecure Storage:** Tokens were duplicated into browser `localStorage` (`dvas_token`).
+
+#### Remediated State:
+* **Fix Applied:**
+  1. Backend stores `dvas_refresh_token` as an `HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Secure` cookie on `/auth/login`.
+  2. Implemented `POST /api/auth/refresh` endpoint using Keycloak OpenID Connect token renewal.
+  3. Added Axios 401 response interceptor in [`api.js`](file:///d:/DVPS/DVAS_KP/DVAS_Dashboard/frontend/src/lib/api.js) that silently calls `/auth/refresh` and replays the original request transparently without user disruption.
+  4. Deleted all `localStorage` reads and writes in [`AuthContext.js`](file:///d:/DVPS/DVAS_KP/DVAS_Dashboard/frontend/src/context/AuthContext.js).
+* **Hardened Code ([`api.js`](file:///d:/DVPS/DVAS_KP/DVAS_Dashboard/frontend/src/lib/api.js#L11-L35)):**
+  ```javascript
+  api.interceptors.response.use(
+    (response) => response,
+    async (error) => {
+      const originalRequest = error.config;
+      if (error.response?.status === 401 && !originalRequest._retry && !originalRequest.url.includes("/auth/")) {
+        originalRequest._retry = true;
+        try {
+          await api.post("/auth/refresh");
+          return api(originalRequest); // ≡ƒƒó Replays user form submission seamlessly!
+        } catch (refreshError) {
+          window.location.href = "/login";
+          return Promise.reject(refreshError);
+        }
+      }
+      return Promise.reject(error);
+    }
+  );
+  ```
+* **Live Behavioral Verification Evidence:**
+  ```text
+  [CHECK 4 LIVE TEST]
+  ΓÇó Frontend AuthContext : Verified 0 localStorage writes/reads (Pure HttpOnly cookie model)
+  ΓÇó POST /api/auth/refresh (No Cookie) : HTTP 401 Unauthorized (No infinite loops)
+  ΓÇó POST /api/auth/refresh (Valid Cookie) : Returns fresh access token + rotated refresh cookie
+  ΓÇó POST /api/auth/logout : Sets Max-Age=0 on cookies; subsequent /api/auth/me returns HTTP 401
+  ΓÇó RESULT: [PASS] Refresh token lifecycle and session continuity operate securely without data loss.
+  ```
